/**
 * Elecrow CrowPanel 7.0" (basic DIS08070H or Advance) — aircraft over my home
 *
 * Left: a north-up radar centred on home with range rings, each aircraft drawn
 * as a heading-rotated icon colored by altitude, with callsign / altitude label
 * and a short trail. Positions are dead-reckoned between polls so they glide.
 * Right: clock, the nearest aircraft (tap one, on the radar or in the list,
 * for details), feed status and range buttons.
 * While no aircraft are airborne within range, the colorclock face is shown
 * instead (background = time as RGB); tap it to peek at the radar.
 *
 * Data source (web UI):
 *   - a local ADS-B receiver (readsb / dump1090 / tar1090 aircraft.json), and/or
 *   - an online aggregator: adsb.lol (default) or airplanes.live (/v2/point/lat/lon/radius);
 *     airplanes.live serves only its feeders (by IP); others get 403 unless approved by email
 *   "Auto" uses the receiver when it answers and falls back to the online feed.
 * Fetching runs in its own task on core 0, so slow HTTPS never stalls drawing.
 *
 * Configurable via web UI at http://overhead.local (or device IP): home
 * location, range, data source, labels / trails, time zone, brightness, dim and
 * off schedules, and the overhead card / beep. Range, brightness, schedules and
 * overhead options are also on screen: tap the top-left and top-right
 * corners within 5 s.
 *
 * Libraries (install via Library Manager):
 *   - LovyanGFX   by lovyan03
 *   - WiFiManager by tzapu
 *   - ArduinoJson by Benoit Blanchon (v7)
 *   (Preferences, WebServer, HTTPClient, ESPmDNS, Wire are built-in to the ESP32 core.)
 *
 * Build as "ESP32S3 Dev Module" with OPI PSRAM (see README.md for full FQBNs).
 * Board selection and all display / touch hardware details live in crowpanel7.h/.cpp.
 */

